# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Recently Played — environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The mockup runs out of the box with ZERO environment variables. The bundled
# sample data in src/lib/sampleHistory.ts is all you need to see the page work.
#
# The variables below only become necessary when you wire up a real data
# source (see docs/data-sources.md for the recipes). Uncomment the ones you
# actually use; leave the rest off.
#
# Never commit the real .env file. The .gitignore already excludes it.


# ─── Database (recipe: docs/data-sources.md#postgres) ────────────────────────
#
# Required if you replace the history stub with a Postgres-backed implementation.
#
# How to get one:
#   • Railway:  one-click "Add Postgres" in your project; DATABASE_URL is
#               wired automatically — you usually won't need to set this by hand.
#   • Vercel:   add a Vercel Postgres or Neon integration; same auto-wiring.
#   • Supabase: project Settings → Database → Connection string (URI).
#   • Neon:     project dashboard → Connection Details → Connection string.
#   • Local:    `docker run -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=dev -p 5432:5432 postgres`
#               then DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:dev@localhost:5432/postgres

# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname


# ─── Last.fm API key (recipe: docs/data-sources.md#lastfm) ───────────────────
#
# Required if you wire the history endpoint to Last.fm.
#
# How to get one:
#   1. Sign up / log in at https://www.last.fm
#   2. Visit https://www.last.fm/api/account/create
#   3. Fill in any application name + description — the form accepts almost
#      anything for personal use. You don't need a callback URL.
#   4. Copy the "API key" value here. The "Shared secret" is only needed
#      for actions that modify a user's account (we only read), so you can
#      ignore it.
#
# The key takes effect immediately; no review or approval is required.

# LASTFM_API_KEY=
# LASTFM_USERNAME=your-lastfm-handle


# ─── Scrobble write endpoint shared secret ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Required if you add a POST /api/scrobble endpoint that external clients
# push to (e.g. the CloweScrobbler iOS app). Treat this like a password —
# anyone who knows it can submit fake scrobbles to your server.
#
# How to generate one:
#   openssl rand -hex 32      # macOS / Linux — pick this one
#   pwgen -s 64 1             # alternative
#
# The exact value doesn't matter; what matters is that it's long, random,
# and only known to you and the apps you authorize. Paste it into both your
# deploy's env AND the scrobbling client's "API Secret" field.

# CRON_SECRET=


# ─── Spotify API (optional, recipe: docs/data-sources.md) ────────────────────
#
# Required only if you wire /api/spotify/search to the real Spotify Web API
# (for exact-match Spotify links per track). The mockup's stub returns null
# and the page falls back gracefully to a generic Spotify search URL.
#
# How to get one:
#   1. Log in at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard
#   2. "Create app" — any name, any description, any redirect URI works for
#      the client-credentials flow this endpoint would use.
#   3. The app page shows your Client ID. Click "View client secret" to
#      reveal the secret.

# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
